    "['load-balance unequal-cost enable', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis overload', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols isis overload\\nset protocols isis traffic-engineering unequal-cost\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent is not a direct 1:1 translation, but achieves similar functionality. Huawei's `load-balance unequal-cost enable` allows IS-IS to use unequal-cost paths for load balancing. In Juniper, this is achieved by:\\n1. First setting IS-IS to allow overload (though not strictly necessary for this function)\\n2. Enabling traffic-engineering with unequal-cost path support\\n\\nThe actual load-balancing behavior would then be controlled by Juniper's routing policy framework.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis overload'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis traffic-engineering unequal-cost', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols isis overload\\nset protocols isis traffic-engineering unequal-cost\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent is not a direct 1:1 translation, but achieves similar functionality. Huawei's `load-balance unequal-cost enable` allows IS-IS to use unequal-cost paths for load balancing. In Juniper, this is achieved by:\\n1. First setting IS-IS to allow overload (though not strictly necessary for this function)\\n2. Enabling traffic-engineering with unequal-cost path support\\n\\nThe actual load-balancing behavior would then be controlled by Juniper's routing policy framework.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis traffic-engineering unequal-cost'}]]": 1,
